<Layout home title="KabuForge — Japanese Equity Research and Backtesting" description="Open-source, local-first Japanese equity research: factors, strategies, backtesting, local paper simulation and MCP interfaces."><p class="eyebrow">OPEN SOURCE · LOCAL FIRST · JAPANESE EQUITIES</p><div class="hero"><div><h1>Reproducible research.<br/>Japanese equities.</h1><p class="lead">Connect factor and strategy research to portfolio targets, risk controls and local simulation. One inspectable pipeline across Python, CLI, desktop and MCP.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/docs/quickstart/">Get started</a><a class="secondary" href="https://github.com/Siyuan-chat/KabuForge">View on GitHub</a></div><p class="version">0.1.1 · tag v0.1.1 · Python 3.12+ · AGPL-3.0-only</p></div><div class="architecture-card"><div class="card-label">DECISION PIPELINE</div><ol><li><b>01</b> Factor <small>Registered research inputs</small></li><li><b>02</b> Strategy <small>Target portfolio</small></li><li><b>03</b> Risk &amp; Planner <small>Constraints and execution quotes</small></li><li><b>04</b> OrderIntent <small>Inspect the plan</small></li></ol><p>Diagram of the public architecture. Not a software screenshot.</p></div></div><section class="home-section"><p class="eyebrow">RESEARCH → PLAN → INSPECT</p><h2>One workflow. Several ways in.</h2><div class="feature-grid"><div><h3>Extend your research</h3><p>Register versioned factors and strategies with validators. Keep research contracts explicit and decisions inspectable.</p><a href="/docs/architecture/">Explore the architecture</a></div><div><h3>Simulate locally</h3><p>Separate research marks from execution quotes. Review historical backtests and local paper journals.</p><a href="/examples/offline-demo/">Run a synthetic example</a></div><div><h3>Use your interface</h3><p>Use shared services through Python, CLI, the desktop workbench or a workspace-bounded MCP agent.</p><a href="/docs/mcp/">Connect an MCP client</a></div></div></section><section class="demo-section"><div><p class="eyebrow">OFFLINE BY DESIGN</p><h2>Your first run needs no API key.</h2><p>The synthetic demo creates fictional inputs for checking configuration, declared PIT fields, risk, order planning and local simulation. Inspect the files it leaves behind.</p><a href="/docs/quickstart/">Follow the complete quickstart</a></div><div class="code"><button type="button" class="copy">Copy</button><pre><code>python -m pip install .
kabuforge doctor
kabuforge demo --out output/demo</code></pre><span class="copy-status" role="status"></span></div></section><section class="boundary"><h2>Know what the result establishes.</h2><p>An availability-time gate is not complete historical PIT certification. Simulated fills are not broker fills. Real order submission is disabled, and synthetic examples cannot establish investment performance.</p><a href="/docs/methodology/">Read the methodology and limitations</a><p class="research-context">Research notes and project context: <a href="https://arcaviso.com/">ArcaViso</a>.</p></section></Layout>